n_title":"Introduction","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:af5e4191adf2d06d78f6d6454e818e0dc541ff25f9bc8dceae2cd831e41d04d0","file":"preprints/Irrational-cubic-fourfolds-with-geometric-K3-categories-September-24-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex","line":224,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"4888e2418f0111afc78b01b5455b8a161e098d06f08fb0fe02cc516074bb1111","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Irrational-cubic-fourfolds-with-geometric-K3-categories-September-24-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:af5e4191adf2d06d78f6d6454e818e0dc541ff25f9bc8dceae2cd831e41d04d0","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Irrational-cubic-fourfolds-with-geometric-K3-categories-September-24-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex#L224"},"statement_kind":"corollary","text":"\\label{cor:associated-k3}\nLet \\(d_0\\) be the threshold in Theorem~\\ref{thm:main}. For every admissible\n\\(d>d_0\\), a very general \\(X\\in\\mathcal C_d\\) is irrational and admits a\nlabelling \\(K\\) of discriminant \\(d\\) and a primitively polarized smooth\nprojective K3 surface \\((S_{\\mathrm{Hdg}},L)\\), with \\(L^2=d\\), for which\nthere is an integral Hodge isometry\n\\[\n K^\\perp \\simeq L^\\perp(-1).\n\\]\nHere \\(L^\\perp\\subset H^2(S_{\\mathrm{Hdg}},\\Z)\\), and the surface cup\npairing is reversed. Thus an associated untwisted polarized K3 surface in\nthis Hodge-theoretic sense is not sufficient for rationality."}
